From 3c06e6468add96c32b9ff760b4ab20a09fce27aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 23:36:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 211/211] Reaper v1.7.4: fix static-DHCP client dropdown
 placement + Wireless theme flash

Two www-only fixes from v1.7.3 on-metal testing:

- static-DHCP client picker (LAN > DHCP Server): the v1.7.2 fix escaped the iframe
  clip by centering the dropdown in the viewport (position:fixed), leaving it
  detached far from the button. Re-anchor it to its own input cell and open it
  UPWARD - overlaying the config already rendered above the input, so the shell
  frame never has to grow (no clip) and it sits on the pull-arrow. Capped height +
  inner scroll for long lists. reaper_content.css.

- Wireless page theme-flash (FOUC): the anti-flash veil failsafe (700ms) lifted
  before heavy/skip-listed stock pages (Wireless, DHCP - no serve-time pre-paint)
  finished loading and got runtime-themed, flashing the stock chrome. Raised to 3s
  so the load-handler themed reveal always wins; the dark stage shows during load,
  never stock. reaper_shell.asp.

version.conf EXTENDNO -> Reaper_v1.7.4.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
